 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask with education",
   "texto": [
    "To ask with courtesy you use **Je voudrais…** (I want, I want). **Je veux** («I want to») may sound too direct in this context.",
    "The waiter asks **Vous désirez ?** (what do you want?) and then **Et avec ça ?** (anything else?). When serving you, says **Voilà** (here you are).",
    "To pay: **Ça fait combien ?** (what is it?) and **L'addition, s'il vous plaît** (the account, please)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Quantities",
   "texto": [
    "With a measured expression, **de** is normally used (no item if a non-specific amount is spoken): **un verre de lait**, **une tasse de thé**, **une bouteille d'eau**.",
    "In front of a vowel, **de** loses the «e» and is written **d'**: **d'eau**.",
    "**à** + article: **au** (masculine), **à la** (feminine), **à l'** (before vocal) or **aux** (plural) is used to indicate the ingredient. Example: **un sandwich au fromage** (a cheese sandwich; **à + le = au**)."
   ]
  },
